invariant: INV-16
file: sha256_hw.c
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: sha256_hw.c drops the target attribute that turns the SHA-256
  instructions on for its own functions, so the file compiles only where
  the whole object is built with the instruction flags, and an object
  built that way may run them in code no CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 bit
  ever chose. The script compiles the file for x86-64 and for arm64 with
  no instruction flag and requires the three entries and the instructions
  there.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#ifdef SHA256_HW_ARM
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("+sha2"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("sha,ssse3,sse4.1"))), apply_to = function)
#endif
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#ifdef SHA256_HW_ARM
#pragma GCC target("+sha2")
#else
#pragma GCC target("sha,ssse3,sse4.1")
#endif
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
